# Paths from which someone can reach the cloud account or the production database, rather
# than just the code.
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" is on in the "protect main" ruleset, so this file now has
# teeth: a pull request touching these paths cannot merge without the owner. Turning that
# setting off silently reduces this file to auto-requesting a reviewer.
#
# The owner is also the only bypass actor on that ruleset, which is deliberate. Nobody else can
# merge a change here at all, and the owner merges their own by bypassing — the alternative,
# a second code owner, is a second person who can reach production.
#
# /.github/ is here for two reasons: it covers this file, and it covers the workflows that hold
# the federated CI identity, where an edit can mint cloud credentials.
#
# /supabase/ is here because a migration is deployed to production by that same pipeline and can
# destroy data no rollback restores — see the expand-then-contract note in the deploy runbook.

/infra/     @abdulqdaer-q
/scripts/   @abdulqdaer-q
/.github/   @abdulqdaer-q
/supabase/  @abdulqdaer-q
